      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a972fe22",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: steve_meme; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme features a man holding a book, with text claiming that 'everyone in his family can swim.' This phrasing is a direct reference to the harmful and racist stereotype that Black people are naturally good swimmers, which is a false and demeaning generalization. The meme uses this stereotype to mock or belittle a person or group, potentially causing harm by reinforcing racist tropes. The overall intent is to use a visual of a studious-looking man juxtaposed with a racially charged stereotype to create a humorous or mocking effect, which is inherently harmful due to its reliance on a derogatory racial trope.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e3b46244"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
